[?2004hroot@86356c506d92:/task# nl -ba /task/input/SOP_takeover.md
[?2004l     1	# SOP-BI-07: Taking over an RNA-seq differential-expression project
     2	
     3	## 1. Principle
     4	The analyst who releases a result is responsible for every number in it. Files left by a previous
     5	analyst (scripts, intermediate tables, drafts) are not raw data. They may be reused only after they
     6	have been verified against the raw data; anything may be recomputed instead. A script is judged by
     7	what it does and a file by what it contains, not by comments, file names or the hand-over note.
     8	
     9	## 2. Identity control of libraries
    10	The gene panel contains sex-chromosome control genes: `XIST` (transcribed in female cells only) and
    11	the Y-linked genes `RPS4Y1`, `DDX3Y`, `KDM5D`, `UTY`, `EIF1AY` (transcribed in male cells only).
    12	
    13	For every FASTQ file, from the reads of that file that are assigned to genes:
    14	- X = number of reads assigned to `XIST`
    15	- Y = number of reads assigned to the five Y-linked genes together
    16	- minor marker share = min(X, Y) / (X + Y)
    17	
    18	Acceptance criterion: a library is accepted as coming from a single donor if its minor marker share
    19	is below 0.02. Its sex is then `F` if X > Y and `M` otherwise.
    20	
    21	A library with a minor marker share of 0.02 or more contains material of more than one donor. Such
    22	a library has no identity: it cannot be assigned to any record of the sample sheet, it is reported
    23	with `inferred_sex` = `mixed`, and it does not enter the statistical model (`condition_used` =
    24	`excluded`).
    25	
    26	Passing this control shows that a library comes from one donor. It does not show that this donor is
    27	the one named in the sample sheet.
    28	
    29	A differential-expression table is released only if every library in the model passed the identity
    30	control and entered the model under the condition its cells actually received. A library that
    31	passed the control and whose data agree with its sample-sheet record is never left out of the model.
    32	
    33	## 3. Audit of the previous analysis
    34	Every item of the checklist below gets a verdict in `audit.tsv`: `ok` if the requirement is met,
    35	`defective` if it is not.
    36	
    37	- Judge every item on its own. A step that is carried out correctly on a faulty input is `ok`; the
    38	  fault belongs to the item that caused it.
    39	- The items concern the files in `previous_analysis/` as shipped (scripts and tables), not your own
    40	  analysis.
    41	- The checklist is complete: nothing else about the previous analysis is rated. In particular, the
    42	  identity control of section 2 was not part of the previous analysis and is not an audit item.
    43	
    44	| item | requirement |
    45	|---|---|
    46	| `quant_library_type` | The library type that `scripts/01_quantify.sh` passes to the quantifier fits the protocol of these libraries, so that no reads are discarded because of their orientation. |
    47	| `merge_read_counts` | `scripts/02_merge_counts.py` builds the gene-level matrix from estimated read counts (not from length- or depth-normalised abundances), summed over all transcripts of a gene. |
    48	| `matrix_sample_files` | Every column of `gene_counts_merged.tsv` was obtained from the FASTQ file that `samples.tsv` lists for the sample in the column header. |
    49	| `matrix_all_reads` | Every column of `gene_counts_merged.tsv` was obtained from all reads of a FASTQ file, not from a part of a file. |
    50	| `de_session_term` | The model in `scripts/03_de.py` contains the library-prep session in addition to the treatment. |
    51	| `de_contrast_direction` | The `log2fc` that `scripts/03_de.py` writes is treated relative to vehicle: positive when expression is higher in treated cells. |
    52	| `de_adjusted_pvalues` | The `padj` that `scripts/03_de.py` writes is the p-value adjusted for multiple testing over the tested genes. |
    53	| `draft_reproducible` | `de_draft.tsv` is the output of `scripts/03_de.py` for `gene_counts_merged.tsv` and `/task/input/samples.tsv` as shipped (the same numbers, apart from rounding in the last printed digit). |
    54	
    55	## 4. Erratum for results that have already left the group
    56	For every gene of a list that was communicated outside the group, `erratum.tsv` states whether the
    57	released analysis supports it: `confirmed` if the gene is differentially expressed in the released
    58	table (`significant` = 1), `retracted` otherwise. Direction and size of an effect are taken from the
    59	released table, not from the erratum.
[?2004hroot@86356c506d92:/task# nl -ba /task/input/lab_notes.md; printf '\n--- samples ---\n'; nl -ba /task/input/samples.tsv
[?2004l     1	# Wet-lab notes: compound vs vehicle, primary cells
     2	
     3	- Cells: primary cells from 12 unrelated donors (one culture per donor), passage 2.
     4	- Treatment: compound at 1 uM or vehicle (0.1% DMSO) for 24 h; one condition per donor.
     5	- RNA: column purification with on-column DNase; RIN >= 8.9 for all samples.
     6	- Gene panel: the transcripts in `reference/` (targeted panel plus sex-chromosome control genes).
     7	- Library prep: poly-A selection, unstranded. Two prep sessions because the first kit lot ran out: 2024-03-05 (6 libraries, kit lot A, operator 1) and 2024-03-19 (6 libraries, kit lot B, operator 2, different PCR cycler). The session of each library is in the sample sheet.
     8	- Sequencing: all libraries pooled equimolar on one lane, 50-cycle single read. The core delivered adapter-trimmed reads; read names and base qualities were stripped to placeholders by their export tool.
     9	- Incident (recorded for completeness): the final libraries were stored at -20 C in a cardboard box. When the box was taken out for pooling, condensation had made the hand-written tube labels partly illegible. All tubes were re-labelled from the box map before pooling and index assignment. Library-prep session and all other sample-sheet fields were copied from the original records.

